* Core specialists always active: GP, Internal Medicine, ER/Red-Flag (baseline debate for common/systemic/urgent).
* Conditional specialists: Pharmacist and Biologist—summoned only when relevant (e.g., meds mentioned, biological clues)—via prompt logic (ADK's LLM decides based on input).
* Researchers: 2 specialized (Studies + Guidelines/Local) for evidence validation during debate (kept simple; we can add more later).
* Debater: Single agent to synthesize/refine.
* Flow: Parallel proposals → conditional summons → debate with evidence → 1-2 iterations → finalized JSON output with disclaimers.


agents/diagnostics/
├── __init__.py                  # Exports main agent
├── agent.py                     # Main DiagnosticAgent (coordinator)
├── specialists/                 # Subfolder for specialists
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── gp.py                    # General Practitioner
│   ├── internal.py              # Internal Medicine
│   ├── er_redflag.py            # ER/Red-Flag
│   ├── pharmacist.py            # Conditional
│   └── biologist.py             # Conditional
├── debater.py                   # Single debater
└── researchers/                 # Researcher
    ├── __init__.py
    ├── studies_researcher.py    # Researcher for studies evidence


This keeps it efficient (core only for most cases) and modular (easy to expand).